    action def DeliveryRunS327 {
        action storyCritPass4;
        verification storyCritPass4DoD : Test { :>> id = "0d800421-0814-6421-9b3e-000000300421"; :>> method = VerificationMethod::analyze; :>> procedureText = "Pass 4: nViewerInProgramEdit, nViewerIterativeCritique, nViewerQueryExpansion, nViewerSeparation, nViewerViewpointForm. 10 fail, 5 pass. MILESTONE, read back from the computed view: Need coverage 18 -> 23 of 39, and `next_targets Need` now reports 0 critiquable with 16 blocked — every Need not authored by claudeOpus5 is critique-covered, and 39 minus 23 is exactly the blocked set. TWO FINDINGS NAME THE SAME UNNOTICED COLLISION: nViewerInProgramEdit wants edit-then-critique on one surface, and nViewerIterativeCritique wants an AI to critique each element along an axis — both run into critique independence, which neither mentions. An edit does not transfer authorship, so a user critiquing what they just edited self-critiques and the coverage computation discards it; and MEASURED, 87 of 154 uncovered elements are claudeOpus5-authored, so an AI iterating an axis would silently fail to count for 56 percent of them. A THIRD FINDING IS A CLAUSE THAT IS TESTABLE AND FALSE: nViewerSeparation says the write API and guards 'remain the ONLY write path', which CLAUDE.md itself contradicts, so a faithful verification must fail permanently on correct behaviour — worse than an untestable clause, because honest verification becomes impossible. validate 355 clean; 34 guards ALL PASS."; }
        part storyCritPass4DoDR1 : TestResult { :>> id = "0d800422-0814-6422-9b3e-000000300422"; :>> outcome = VerdictKind::pass; :>> judgedAgainst = "13f825e"; :>> judgedAt = "2026-08-17"; :>> judgedBy = "claudeOpus5"; }
    }

    verification c4RefineGate : Test { :>> id = "0d800423-0814-6423-9b3e-000000300423"; :>> title = "Sprint 327 refine gate (DoR)"; :>> createdAt = "2026-08-17"; :>> createdBy = "claudeOpus5"; :>> method = VerificationMethod::inspect; :>> procedureText = "DoR. The last five critiquable Needs, all keel-viewer. Two factual claims were checked before writing: that `keel render` still accepts exactly three modes (it does — main.rs and the view.rs dispatch), and that the architecture question N-6 presents as open has been answered (D0114 chose a shape and D0152 superseded it, #Supersede edge at 0152 line 24). Both checks changed what the critiques say. estimatedPoints=3."; }
