    part c4CloseOutGateR1 : TestResult { :>> id = "0d80042c-0814-642c-9b3e-00000030042c"; :>> outcome = VerdictKind::pass; :>> judgedAgainst = "13f825e"; :>> judgedAt = "2026-08-17"; :>> judgedBy = "claudeOpus5"; }

    verification c4RetroGate : Test { :>> id = "0d80042d-0814-642d-9b3e-00000030042d"; :>> title = "Sprint 327 retro gate (autonomous, D0049)"; :>> createdAt = "2026-08-17"; :>> createdBy = "claudeOpus5"; :>> method = VerificationMethod::analyze; :>> procedureText = "Autonomous retro (D0049) under D0131's retroTrack, covering the four-pass Needs backfill as a unit. WELL: (1) measuring the independence split first meant zero wasted critiques across 60 lenses; (2) checking factual claims before writing them caught two that were false, and the checks are recorded inside the passes so a reader inherits the correction; (3) the cross-Need findings — the independence collision and the deferred-criteria chain — could only surface by working a corpus with the measurement in hand, which is the case for doing this as a sequence of passes rather than element by element on demand. AVOIDABLE-ISSUE across the four passes: one tool defect (the helper's two-bug author lookup, pass 2) and one shell-quoting failure (pass 1), both already-recorded classes, both caught before they reached the model. WHAT I WOULD DO DIFFERENTLY: pass 1 wrote 14 fails of 15 and its rigor self-check came only in the review gate; the later passes checked claims BEFORE writing, which is both cheaper and more honest. The ordering of that check is the lesson, not its existence. Estimate 3 pts, delivered — 12 pts across the four passes against 12 estimated."; }
